fixes.react:
Implement state management to control auto-updates. Use React hooks to manage the timing and provide user controls:
const [isPaused, setIsPaused] = useState(false);
const pauseUpdates = () => setIsPaused(true);
const resumeUpdates = () => setIsPaused(false);

fixes.vue:
Use Vue's reactivity system to manage auto-updates and provide user controls:
<template>
  <button @click="pauseUpdates">Pause</button>
  <button @click="resumeUpdates">Resume</button>
</template>
<script>
export default {
  data() {
    return { isPaused: false };
  },
  methods: {
    pauseUpdates() { this.isPaused = true; },
    resumeUpdates() { this.isPaused = false; }
  }
};
</script>

fixes.angular:
Use Angular's component lifecycle and event binding to manage auto-updates and provide user controls:
<template>
  <button (click)="pauseUpdates()">Pause</button>
  <button (click)="resumeUpdates()">Resume</button>
</template>
<script>
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
@Component({
  selector: 'app-auto-update',
  templateUrl: './auto-update.component.html'
})
export class AutoUpdateComponent {
  isPaused = false;
  pauseUpdates() { this.isPaused = true; }
  resumeUpdates() { this.isPaused = false; }
}
</script>

fixes.vanilla:
Use the Reduced Motion Media Query to disable animations for users who prefer reduced motion.
Example:
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .animated-element {
    animation: none;
  }
}

fixes.react:
Use the Reduced Motion Media Query within CSS-in-JS or styled-components to conditionally apply styles.
Example:
const AnimatedElement = styled.div`
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    animation: none;
  }
`;

fixes.vue:
Use the Reduced Motion Media Query within Vue's scoped styles or CSS-in-JS libraries.
Example:
<style scoped>
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .animated-element {
    animation: none;
  }
}
</style>

fixes.angular:
Use the Reduced Motion Media Query within Angular's component styles or global styles.
Example:
@Component({
  styles: [`
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .animated-element {
        animation: none;
      }
    }
  `]
})

